From 40887580c162818fa0e0178c94b9b811ffae2d86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "wilfred.dore" <wilfred.dore@telecom-paristech.org>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:47:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] outings: cite visit facts by exact field key and matching
 value

Linkup returned facts labelled in natural French ("effectif maximal
groupe scolaire", ...). _search_visit only kept a top-level value when
a citation's field equalled its English key, so all seven values became
null even though eight official excerpts were present. A value was also
kept when any citation named its key, whatever the cited value.

- VisitFact.field is now an enum of the seven top-level keys, and the
  query asks for exact keys and values.
- A returned fact with another label stays as a source but supports no
  field. Labels are never mapped by guesswork.
- A value is kept only if every official citation of its key states that
  same value (strict types; prices compared as decimal EUR). Otherwise it
  stays unknown and is listed in unsupported_fields; never zero.
- Tests: the schema enum, a real-shape French-labelled answer, and
  matching vs contradictory values.

Co-Authored-By: Devin AI <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
